(5. DEFICIENCY MANAGEMENT) Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(Every deficiency request must be precise, relevant and tracked.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(CLM-5.1  Single consolidated request) Tj
T*
(   Where practicable, issue one consolidated list identifying each missing or unclear item) Tj
T*
(   and why it is required.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(CLM-5.2  Response window) Tj
T*
(   The demonstration workflow allows fifteen calendar days for response, with reasonable) Tj
T*
(   extension where justified. Production timelines must match current law and contract.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(CLM-5.3  No irrelevant demand) Tj
T*
(   Do not request unrelated historical records, full employment files or excessive identity) Tj
T*
(   documents without a recorded necessity.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(CLM-5.4  Repeated request control) Tj
T*
(   A previously supplied document must not be requested again unless it is unreadable,) Tj
T*
(   incomplete or inconsistent; the reason must be recorded.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(CLM-5.5  Closure) Tj
T*
(   A claim may be administratively closed after documented reminders and review, but must be) Tj
T*
(   reopened where policy or law requires upon receipt of evidence.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
